# Sandbox-image rebuild epoch.
#
# The GHCR tag for each sandbox image is CONTENT-ADDRESSED: sha256(this file + the tool name +
# that tool's Dockerfile), truncated. CI (.github/workflows/sandbox-images.yml) skips the build
# entirely when that tag already exists in GHCR, which is what keeps ~1.7GiB of coding CLIs off
# the critical path of every app release — they change on the order of once a month, releases
# happen several times a week.
#
# BUMP THIS INTEGER to force a rebuild of ALL FOUR images when nothing in a Dockerfile changed
# but the resulting bytes should:
#   - a base-image security refresh (`node:24-bookworm-slim` is a MOVING tag — a Debian CVE fix
#     lands there with no diff here);
#   - the cursor image's installer (`https://cursor.com/install`) is an unpinned remote script, so
#     it is the one CLI whose version cannot be pinned from the Dockerfile at all.
# A version bump inside a Dockerfile (CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION, COPILOT_CLI_VERSION, …) needs NO epoch
# bump — that already changes the file, hence the hash, hence the tag.
#
# Bumping is a reviewable commit, on purpose: a rebuild replaces the bytes that run with the host
# Docker socket in reach, so it should never be a side effect of an unrelated release.
EPOCH=1
